    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.map\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice to be able to set the window height for the MiniMap, as currently the window is the full height of the Neovim window.\r\nThis causes the `winblend` to get applied to anything \"behind\" the map window, even when there is no part of the map on that line.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e214bdc0-8811-4356-a0ac-f5efc561561c)\r\nI have set my cursor line to white to demonstrate the effect.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to be able to, for example set the height of the map window to the \"text height\" of its contents.\r\ne.g.\r\n```lua\r\nwindow.height = vim.api.nvim_win_text_height(MiniMap.current.win_data[1], {}).all\r\n```\r\nWhich currently has no effect when put in the config for mini.map, as the height is forced.\r\n```lua\r\n-- In function H.normalize_window_options\r\nheight = vim.o.lines - vim.o.cmdheight - (has_tabline and 1 or 0) - (has_statusline and 1 or 0),\r\n```\r\n[See source@mini.map:1357-1382](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.map/blob/8baf542570cbff05b568958d20e3f842bd941545/lua/mini/map.lua#L1357-L1382)\r\nAs such, setting `window.height` currently seem to have no effect.",
    "closed_at": "2024-09-05T11:07:12Z",
